From: Stanislaw Pal <kuncy7@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] DEBUG: ath11k: nss: trace the events the firmware sends us

The host->firmware direction of the wifili control channel has been
traced since E27, but nothing ever logged the opposite direction, so
"the firmware never sends X" was never actually measured.

Log every incoming event, and in particular whether the firmware asks
the host to set up the per-TID reorder queues of a freshly created
peer - NSS_WIFILI_TID_REOQ_SETUP_MSG, whose handler is an empty stub
in this driver and for which no sender exists at all.

DEBUG ONLY - do not submit.

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/nss.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/nss.c
@@ -364,6 +364,16 @@
 	ath11k_dbg(ab, ATH11K_DBG_NSS, "nss wifili event received %d response %d error %d\n",
 		   msg_type, response, error);
 
+	/* DEBUG E62a: the host->firmware direction has been traced since
+	 * E27, the firmware->host direction never was. Log every incoming
+	 * event unconditionally, skipping only the two statistics syncs
+	 * that could flood the console.
+	 */
+	if (msg_type != NSS_WIFILI_STATS_MSG &&
+	    msg_type != NSS_WIFILI_PEER_STATS_MSG)
+		pr_info("nss-evt: type=%u resp=%u err=%u\n",
+			msg_type, response, error);
+
 	switch (msg_type) {
 	case NSS_WIFILI_INIT_MSG:
 	case NSS_WIFILI_PDEV_INIT_MSG:
@@ -422,6 +432,12 @@
 		ath11k_nss_get_peer_stats(ab, peer_stats);
 		break;
 	case NSS_WIFILI_TID_REOQ_SETUP_MSG:
+		/* DEBUG E62a: does the firmware ask us to set up the per-TID
+		 * reorder queues? There has never been a sender for this
+		 * message on our side, and this stub swallows any request.
+		 */
+		pr_info("nss-evt: *** TID_REOQ_SETUP tid=%u peer_id=%u *** (stub, brak obslugi)\n",
+			msg->msg.reotidqmsg.tid, msg->msg.reotidqmsg.peer_id);
 		/* TODO setup tidq */
 		break;
 	case NSS_WIFILI_WDS_PEER_ADD_MSG:
